\subsection{Implementation details and reproducibility}
\label{sec:impl}
All experiments run on a single NVIDIA T4 GPU (15.6\,GB) on Google Colab,
with occasional A100~(40\,GB) sessions for diagnostic comparison.
Code is in PyTorch~\citep{paszke2019pytorch} using the
HuggingFace~\texttt{diffusers}~\citep{vonplaten2022diffusers}
\texttt{AutoencoderKL}. The forecaster's {Earthformer-UNet} uses gradient
checkpointing to fit at $\mathit{hidden}=128,\ n\_blocks=2,\
\mathrm{batch\_size}=2$.

\paragraph{Parameter counts.}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
\item \texttt{AutoencoderKL} (full VAE): $\sim 83.65$\,M parameters.
\item \textsc{FlowCast}/\textsc{DiffCast} forecaster on T4
      ($\mathit{hidden}=128,\ n\_blocks=2$): $\sim 8.97$\,M parameters.
\item Paper-spec forecaster ($\mathit{hidden}=192,\ n\_blocks=4$) on
      A100: $\sim 28$\,M parameters; not used for our headline numbers.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Software stack.} Python~3.12; PyTorch~2.x (Colab default);
HuggingFace \texttt{diffusers}~\citep{vonplaten2022diffusers};
\texttt{lpips}~$0.1.4$; \texttt{tifffile}; \texttt{scikit-image}; CUDA~12.x.

\paragraph{Random seeds.} CFM training and EDM training both seed PyTorch
and NumPy with \texttt{seed=42}; the DiffCast pair-dataset builder uses
\texttt{seed=42} as the base for per-rollout reseeding (effective seed
$= 42 + 1000 \cdot \mathrm{day\_idx} + \mathrm{sample\_idx}$); the LPIPS
network is initialised deterministically by \texttt{lpips} (effective
\texttt{seed=0}).

\paragraph{Code artifact.} The full implementation
(\texttt{src/}~ConvLSTM baseline, \texttt{flowcast/}~CFM pipeline,
\texttt{diffcast/}~EDM pipeline), per-channel configs
(\texttt{vis/config\_*.yaml}, \texttt{wv/config\_*.yaml}), two
Colab runner notebooks (\texttt{flowcast/colab\_pipeline.ipynb},
\texttt{diffcast/colab\_pipeline.ipynb}), training/forecast scripts,
snapshot tooling, and automated accuracy-report generation
(\cref{sec:accuracy-report}) are released alongside this paper.

\paragraph{Wall-clock budget (single T4).} \cref{tab:walltime} summarises
the compute required end-to-end on a free Colab T4. The A100 column gives
practical scaling estimates from one diagnostic A100 session.

